From 20bcbcc2895e0b465eb9deea6ecfa2c315e37fd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:47:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Zero-copy presentation: the GS's frames shared with the
 window's OpenGL

At 4x the picture (2560x1792, 18 MB) went GPU -> host memory -> per-pixel
conversion -> glTexSubImage2D every frame, which capped 4x at about 84
frames/s (the swap blocked 10 ms per frame behind the upload).

Now eye 0 (and eye 1 in VR stereo) is blitted into one of five exportable
Vulkan images per eye (Granite external memory, dedicated allocation, plus
an exported binary semaphore signalled after the blit, the image released
to the external queue family). ga2_zerocopy imports them once per image
with GL_EXT_memory_object/_semaphore (_fd on Linux, _win32 on Windows),
waits on the semaphore with glWaitSemaphoreEXT and samples the texture in
place; a GL fence decides when an image goes back to the GS. Frames the
window never showed are waited on and released too. The readback ring
(three -> five slots: zero copy holds the shown image until its fence
passes) still delivers a native-size copy (scaled to at most 1024 wide)
for the mouse menus, frame signatures and shots.

The readback path stays: GA2_PGS_ZERO_COPY=0, no extension, a different
GPU (device UUID compared), the jittered 8x mode, and the HUD panel layer.
GA2_PRESENT_SHOTS=<dir>@<s>,... writes the texture about to be drawn for
the first frame at or after each game time, in either mode.

RTX 4090, gamescope headless 2560x1440 (research/run59/gpu-175): 4x cap
175: title/load screens 174.8 made / 174.4 shown per second (was 90), ship
map 120 with no drops (was 84; now CPU-bound like 1x), GPU 48 %, swap
0.09 ms. GA2_FREERUN runs: the presented 2560x1792 picture is identical to
the readback path's at 7 game times (title, load screen, ship map).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
